Match a worksheet's relationship id regardless of XML namespace prefix.

xlsx_sheets() worked on every fixture, but opening a worksheet by name did
not on all of them: main_sheet_get_relid_expat_callback_element_start looked
the relationship id up as the literal attribute name "r:id".

The prefix is not fixed. ECMA-376 binds the relationship attribute to the
namespace http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/officeDocument/2006/relationships,
and a producer may bind that URI to any prefix it likes. The readxl fixture
nonstandard-xml-ns-prefix.xlsx declares it as "ns", so its <sheet> elements
carry ns:id and the lookup returned NULL, leaving sheetrelid unset and the
worksheet unreachable.

xlsxio already has the tool for this. It parses without namespace processing
(XML_ParserCreate(NULL)) and compares names with XML_Char_icmp_ins(), which
matches a bare name against any "prefix:name", and get_expat_attr_by_name()
uses that comparison. Asking for "id" therefore matches r:id, ns:id and a
bare id alike; asking for "r:id" only ever matches the one spelling.

Note this is the attribute-name arm of a fix upstream already made for the
element name on the same line of reasoning, and it is the same lookup the
adjacent list-sheets callback has carried commented out since 0.2.36.

Limitation, unchanged by this patch: because parsing is prefix-based rather
than namespace-aware, a workbook that binds "r" to some other URI would still
match. Nothing in the corpus does, and fixing it properly means turning on
namespace processing across the whole reader, which is an upstream change.

Origin: written for zuxlsx. Not upstream.
Applies to xlsxio 0.2.36 with 0001-miniz-zip-backend.patch already applied.

--- a/lib/xlsxio_read.c
+++ b/lib/xlsxio_read.c
@@ -903,7 +903,7 @@
   if (XML_Char_icmp_ins(name, X("sheet")) == 0) {
     const XML_Char* sheetname;
     if ((sheetname = get_expat_attr_by_name(atts, X("name"))) != NULL && (!data->sheetname || XML_Char_icmp(sheetname, data->sheetname) == 0)) {
-      const XML_Char* relid = get_expat_attr_by_name(atts, X("r:id"));
+      const XML_Char* relid = get_expat_attr_by_name(atts, X("id"));
       if (relid && *relid) {
         data->sheetrelid = XML_Char_dup(relid);
         XML_StopParser(data->xmlparser, XML_FALSE);
